From f18316b86e5a336d27fecb88a69e50fd68a269dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scroll Ash Lab <scrollash.lab@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 11:31:40 -1000
Subject: [PATCH] tifxyz: apply open-data original_volume_downscale to
 tifxyz_normalized meshes

In the open-data bucket the tifxyz_normalized mesh of 112 of 323 segments
(PHercParis4 x4, PHerc0139 x4, PHerc0500P2 x2; catalog of 2026-10-07) is
stored at 1/original_volume_downscale of the segment's original volume. The
factor is in the bucket catalog (metadata.json, segment
properties.original_volume_downscale); the mesh's meta.json does not carry it,
and vesuvius.tifxyz had no way to apply it, so read_tifxyz returned
coordinates that are centimetres off in the original volume. VC3D's Open
Data cache already applies the factor; this brings the Python reader level.

- read_tifxyz(path, downscale=s): multiply valid coordinates by s via the
  existing Tifxyz.retarget(1/s) (bbox recomputed, grid scale divided by s)
  and record extra["original_volume_downscale_applied"]. A mesh carrying
  that marker, or VC3D's vc_open_data_coordinates_scaled_to_original_volume,
  is never scaled again (downscale != 1 raises).
- vesuvius.tifxyz.open_data: original_volume_downscale(catalog, sample,
  segment) reads the catalog field (segment id or long_id; plain or gzip
  metadata.json), read_open_data_normalized(path, catalog) infers
  sample/segment from the bucket layout and applies the factor.
- Without downscale=, reading a .../mesh/intermediate/tifxyz_normalized
  directory emits OpenDataDownscaleWarning; downscale=1 silences it.
  Default behaviour is otherwise unchanged.

Related: #1734 (catalog bbox through the downscale), #1522, #1727.
